# Lab BT Host (.108) — Standard + First Checks

## STANDARD topology (default — always restore this)

Canonical write-up: `docs/analysis/LAB_STANDARD_TOPOLOGY_20261122.md`  
Proof 2026-11-22: ACL + RFCOMM ch6 `.87`↔`.131` OK.

| Role | Device | BD | Air name | CoD | Power |
|------|--------|-----|----------|-----|-------|
| **Lab HU** | ESP `.131` | `C8:C9:A3:CB:7B:0A` | **BMW 38304** | `0x340408` | ON, discoverable, pairable |
| **Lab Phone** | ESP `.87` | `C8:C9:A3:CB:37:96` | **BT-Analyzer-Phone** | phone | ON for dual-ESP / B3; else off |
| **USB dongle** | `.108` | `C0:B8:83:34:F4:62` | PhoneUSB | — | **OFF** — never discoverable in HU-lab mode |
| CSR | optional | `00:1A:7D:DA:71:02` | — | — | only when explicitly testing |

**Must run**

- Bridge `.131`: `hci_tcp_bridge.py …131 --local-name "BMW 38304"`
- Bridge `.87` (when used): `--local-name "BT-Analyzer-Phone"`
- Pair agent **only** those two BDs — **do not** register PhoneUSB
- Lab HU stack: `bcl_dummy_hu_agent.py hu --hu-profile f20_sim --channel 6`
- iDriveSim **off** (ch6 xor); drop-ins `idrivesim-*.conf` in `.d.off/`
- ESP both: `wifi_ps=none`

**Do not** leave PhoneUSB powered with auto-confirm agent — iPhone will pair to the wrong adapter (2026-11-22).

## Smoking guns (host first — not RF/OTA)

1. **Orphan alias pin:** `/tmp/bcl_dummy/alias_pin_persist.log` — abandoned `python3 -` can force **BMW 38304 on phone hci** forever.  
   `fuser -k /tmp/bcl_dummy/alias_pin_persist.log`
2. Other loops: `cod_pin_home.log`, `cod_pin_home_fast.log`, `phone87_hold.log` — Alias BMW↔Phone + car CoD on phone.
3. **Stale `hci_tcp_bridge`** after ESP reboot → `hci1 removed` / mid-connect drop. Restart bridges only after ESP `/api/status` ready.
4. BlueZ **Alias ≠ HCI Name**; only one powered **BMW 38304**.
5. **PhoneUSB** discoverable + pair-agent `always` → phone pairs to USB, not BMW.
6. CoD drift: inquiry shows `0x400104` (PC) while Alias says BMW — re-`Write Class Device` `0x340408` (+ soft reset if sticky).

## iDriveSim ↔ bt-analyzer resource conflict

**Konflikt:** Beide wollen RFCOMM **ch6** + BMW-Identität / Pair-Agent-Drop-Ins — nie parallel.

| Ressource | iDriveSim | bt-analyzer Lab (`f20_sim`) |
|-----------|-----------|------------------------------|
| RFCOMM ch6 | `idrivesim-rfcomm-bridge.service` (Unit oft auf **`.87`**) | `bcl_dummy_hu_agent.py hu --hu-profile f20_sim` |
| Pair-Agent | Drop-Ins `idrivesim-hu.conf` / `idrivesim-csr.conf` | `bmw-alias.conf` — BMW nur **`.131`**, `.87`=Phone |
| Symptom wenn falsch | Lab: `failed to register accept channel 6`; Phone sieht mehrere BMW / falschen Adapter | — |

**→ Lab (Phone → `.131` / f20_sim):**

```bash
systemctl stop idrivesim-rfcomm-bridge.service
pkill -f /opt/idrivesim/ || true
mkdir -p /etc/systemd/system/bt-pair-agent.service.d.off
mv /etc/systemd/system/bt-pair-agent.service.d/idrivesim-*.conf \
   /etc/systemd/system/bt-pair-agent.service.d.off/ 2>/dev/null || true
systemctl daemon-reload
# dann nur .131 = BMW 38304 powered; ch6 frei für bcl_dummy_hu_agent
# PhoneUSB down; pair-agent ohne F4:62
```

**→ iDriveSim:** `bcl_dummy_hu_agent` stoppen, `idrivesim-*.conf` zurück nach `service.d/`, `systemctl restart idrivesim-rfcomm-bridge bt-pair-agent`.

**Regel:** ch6 = idrivesim **xor** `bcl_dummy_hu_agent` — nie beide.

